   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law, in relation to the operation of commercial casinos",
    "basePrintNo": "S5377",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5377-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1339, RWB L",
    "lawSection": "Racing, Pari-Mutuel Wagering and Breeding Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5377\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and\nbreeding law, in relation to the operation of commercial casinos\n\n PURPOSE OF THE BILL :\n\nThis bill would clarify the permissibility of credit to patrons at\ncommercial casinos.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of the bill would amend Racing, Pari-mutuel wagering and\nBreeding Law § 1339 to clarify that cashing checks is permitted\npursuant to the requirements of subdivisions two through eight of that\nsection, and permit gaming facility licensees to offer other forms of\ncredit to patrons if done so according to the rules of the Gaming\nCommission.\n\nSection 2 of the bill would make the bill effective immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe ability of commercial casinos to extend credit to players taking\npart in gaming activity is an important component of commercial casino\noperations. The law should provide that such credit is permissible, so\nlong as it is done pursuant to rules promulgated by the Gaming\nCommission.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nA similar version of this bill passed the Senate in 2016 (S.8031).\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nThe provision of credit to casino gaming players is expected to\nincrease casino gross gaming revenue, which would increase tax revenue\nto the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
